```
Reason:
The loop above propagates all Oozie configuration properties (matching the regex `^oozie\\..+`) to Beeline, including the `oozie.hive2.*` properties, which can lead to unintended configurations affecting Beeline's behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
for (Map.Entry<String, String> oozieConfig : actionConf.getValByRegex("^oozie\\.(?!launcher|hive2).+").entrySet()) {
    arguments.add("--hiveconf");
    arguments.add(oozieConfig.getKey() + "=" + oozieConfig.getValue());
}
```
Reason:
The updated regex `^oozie\\.(?!launcher|hive2).+` ensures that both `oozie.launcher.*` and `oozie.hive2.*` properties are excluded from being propagated to Beeline, thereby preventing unintended configurations from affecting its execution.

